THE UNITY STATEMENT (the same two-regime map at two scales):
  ENVELOPE (streaming) -- CLUSTER 3-5 R500: 0.553  |  MW 2-4 r_M: 0.565 +- 0.057
  CORE (near-isotropic) -- CLUSTER 0.5-1.5 R500: 0.063  |  MW r<r_M stellar: 0.682 +- 0.036

VERDICTS:
  V1 [MW beta(r) vs the prediction] -- the ENVELOPE (2-4 r_M, 20-40 kpc) is CONFIRMED: b_w = 0.565 +- 0.057 sits INSIDE the 0.4-0.6 band (z = +0.56); the per-bin plateau bins 2-3 and 3-4 both PASS.  The CORE (r<r_M, 5-10 kpc) reading of near-isotropy (0.05-0.1) is REJECTED by the direct stellar-tracer data: b_w = 0.682 +- 0.036, z = +13.86 (the inner halo tracers are already radially anisotropic).  The predicted monotone rise from a near-isotropic core is NOT seen; the measured profile is roughly FLAT at 0.5-0.7 across 5-40 kpc with no low core.
  V2 [scale-unity] -- the STREAMING ENVELOPE regime is measured at BOTH scales with consistent values: cluster 3-5 R500 = 0.553, MW 2-4 r_M = 0.565 +- 0.057 (both in the 0.4-0.6 envelope class).  The EQUILIBRIUM CORE regime is confirmed at CLUSTER scale (0.03-0.09 at 0.5-1.5 R500, G209) but NOT at galaxy scale on the published stellar tracers (0.5-0.9 at 5-10 kpc).  The unity claim is therefore CONFIRMED FOR THE ENVELOPE and UNRESOLVED FOR THE CORE.
  V3 [honest statement] -- the two-regime kinematic map: confirmed at both scales for the streaming envelope (cluster 0.545-0.560 at 3-5 R500; MW 0.565+-0.057 at 2-4 r_M, z=+0.56), but the MW CORE reading is where the galaxy-side data stands AGAINST the prediction (b_w = 0.682+-0.036 vs 0.05-0.1, z=+13.86).  The standard explanation is COMPOSITION: the inner MW halo is 50-80% Gaia-Sausage/Enceladus debris (beta~0.9) + an isotropic remainder (~0-0.3) (Iorio & Belokurov 2021; Lancaster et al. 2019), with thick-disk contamination below 10 kpc (DESI MWS 2026).  Even the isotropic remainder (~0.3) sits ABOVE the 0.05-0.1 band, so the stellar tracers do NOT directly confirm the MW equilibrium-core reading -- the DARK component's beta(r) inside r_M is UNMEASURED by the published tracer samples. The far envelope (r>40-100 kpc) also DIVERGES from the cluster-side continued rise: the published stellar beta DECLINES (Bird+19 <0.3 at 100 kpc; the accreted-isotropic component dominates), so the outer stellar halo is not a clean probe of the dark streaming envelope either.  NET: the MW envelope is confirmed, the MW core is PENDING/CONTRADICTED-on-tracers -- the two-regime map at galaxy scale is only HALF-verified by the existing halo-tracer data, complete verification needs the dark/equilibrium component isolated (composition-decomposed Jeans modelling, cf. G217's sample plan).
  [honesty] ALL MW beta points are published values with citations; flagged D where figure-read/derived; none manufactured.  The in-repo registers hold the CLUSTER-side numbers (G209/G203/G206/G170/G188); the MW halo-tracer points are literature values (VERIFIED/UNVERIFIED per point), not committed data files.
